# ANALYSIS (restart-free DNS + 50ms handshake poll, branch HEAD)
# Design: resolvfile repointed (staged uci) at managed file
# /tmp/resolv.conf.d/nym-resolv.conf; connect/disconnect are rename(2)
# writes reloaded by dnsmasq inotify + ubus-HUP cache flush. Single
# daemon-lifetime actor owns the file; 5s WAN mirror while disconnected.
# One dnsmasq restart at first daemon start ever (converge conditional).
#
# Cycle totals (time nym-vpnc connect -w, 3s disconnect gaps):
#   smoke(cold): 4.46s | c1: 27.66s* | c2: 5.56s | c3: 3.54s
#   c4: 4.75s | c5: 2.19s | c6: 2.60s
#   * c1 = dead exit gateway (92.112.192.97): probes failed ~22s, state
#     machine retried with new gateways, try#1 itself took 3.8s. Noted
#     per protocol as gateway flakiness, not client cost.
#   Registration remains the wildcard: c2 3.99s, c3 2.49s, c5/c6 ~1.3-1.9s.
#
# DNS tail: GONE. "Configured dnsmasq" and "Connected" log in the same
# millisecond (was 3.3s apart). dnsmasq wrapper PID stable across all
# connects/disconnects/daemon crashes (2618796 through 12+ cycles until a
# deliberate third-party restart test).
# Handshake waits: 357/408/562/716ms = actual handshake, detection <=50ms.
#
# Four-way comparison (means, typical cycles):
#   pre-gate  (3969d36, no gate):  total ~11.5s
#   post-gate (3969d36 + gate):    total ~11.7s (rekey floor)
#   post-bump (a89bba82 + gate):   total ~6.4s  (500ms hs quantize + 3.3s dns)
#   this HEAD (dns + 50ms poll):   total 2.2-5.6s, 2.2-2.6s on clean
#                                  registrations — target 2.5-3s met;
#                                  registration variance is the remainder.
#
# Validation battery (all PASS, evidence in session log):
#   A1 PID stability  A2 LAN resolution both states  A3 mirror+inotify
#   A4 single-writer guard (WAN edit while connected never leaks)
#   A5 kill -9 recovery, no restart, no marker files
#   A6 crashloop guard (3x kill/start, PID stable)
#   A7 third-party dnsmasq restart survival (staged delta regenerates)
